WHPX leaves a memory section that is not page aligned alone. Such a
section cannot be mapped as RAM, so whpx_set_phys_mem() turned it into
WHvUnmapGpaRange() of a range it never mapped, which fails, and QEMU
aborted ("WHPX: failed to unmap GPA range"). tpm-crb's command buffer
(RAM at 0xFED40080) and its 1 KiB tpm-ppi region are such, so a
Windows 11 machine with its TPM could not start under WHPX at all
(track M20 step 5). Its accesses trap as MMIO, as before. The same as
patch 82 for HVF. Drop when upstream skips unaligned sections in
whpx_set_phys_mem().

diff --git a/accel/whpx/whpx-common.c b/accel/whpx/whpx-common.c
index 1e851b4..e75efac 100644
--- a/accel/whpx/whpx-common.c
+++ b/accel/whpx/whpx-common.c
@@ -307,8 +307,13 @@ static void whpx_set_phys_mem(MemoryRegionSection *section, bool add)
 
     if (!QEMU_IS_ALIGNED(size, page_size) ||
         !QEMU_IS_ALIGNED(gva, page_size)) {
-        /* Not page aligned, so we can not map as RAM */
-        add = false;
+        /*
+         * Not page aligned, so we can not map as RAM, and it was never
+         * mapped: unmapping it fails (and aborts). Its accesses trap as
+         * MMIO. tpm-crb's command buffer and its tpm-ppi region are such
+         * (2ksbox patch 89, as patch 82 for HVF).
+         */
+        return;
     }
 
     if (!add) {
